# The UNCOVERED ceiling. conformance/gates fails if the ledger's UNCOVERED count RISES above it.
#
# Why a checked-in number and not just a printed one: a printed count is something you can
# stop reading. This one has to be edited by hand, in a commit, which makes progress and
# regression both visible in the diff — and makes "the corpus quietly shrank" impossible,
# because deleting a test raises the count and breaks the build.
#
# LOWER it whenever coverage lands.
#
# RAISE it only when the count rose because hidden work became VISIBLE — a section moving out
# of N/A into UNCOVERED. Never to accommodate a test that was deleted, a marker that was
# dropped, or a section reclassified out of COVERED: those mean coverage was LOST, and each
# wants explaining rather than absorbing. The distinction is the whole point, so a raise
# carries its reason here.
#
