# reference to a field inherited from two interfaces, which §6.4.2 makes a compile-time error
# ("An attempt to refer to any of the fields by its simple name results in a compile-time
# error"). find_field returned the first match and stopped. The check counts DISTINCT
# declarations reachable through interfaces, stops at the first class that declares the name
# (§8.3 hiding), and is deliberately restricted to the interface case the section states — a
# superclass field clashing with an interface constant is a different question this does not
# answer, and inventing a rule for it is what §15.24's "common supertype" was.
